<urn:usf:requirement:provider-availability-tuple> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Classify every configured route by requested route, underlying model, adapter, credential name, capability, privacy, catalogue price, entitlement, quota, health, actual identity and probe freshness; partition all exclusions and preserve unknown distinct from zero." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-availability-tuple> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-catalogue-freeze> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Fetch bounded models.dev data only on explicit refresh, preserve exact raw bytes and a deterministic normalized view with separate digests, installed adapter versions and named denominators, and never maintain a hand-curated model roster." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-catalogue-freeze> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-command-surface> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Implement doctor, models, probe and route through the static USF command registry with documented bounded subcommands, stable JSON, explicit external-contact and mutation effects, and no operational dependence on ad hoc scripts." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-command-surface> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-concurrency-refusal> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Validate every host and provider concurrency bound as a positive finite safe integer before scheduling; refuse malformed bounds without provider contact, empty batches or nontermination." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-concurrency-refusal> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Read only explicitly selected .env files with owner-only mode through an exact per-route credential-name allowlist; never copy, print, digest, persist or wholesale export credential values, and keep adapter state beneath USF_PROVIDER_HOME." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-credential-containment> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-probe-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Contact only explicitly selected direct maintained adapters after preflight eligibility, with a fixed public-safe prompt, bounded routes, wall time and tokens, maximum paid cost zero, no fallback, sanitized errors, and recorded requested and actual identity, usage, quota signal and cost evidence." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-probe-boundary> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-route-purity> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Route without provider contact from exact work, policy, catalogue and fresh probe digests; consider every configured route, explain each inclusion and exclusion, apply declared host and provider caps, and make the same inputs byte-repeatable." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-route-purity> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-semantic-task-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Qualify the exact provider, requested and actual model, adapter, auth mode, tool profile, prompt version, context config and output config for one task class against a versioned suite and corpus with deterministic dimension thresholds; missing answers score zero, default is unqualified, results are time-bounded and derived role labels grant no authority or permanent admission." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-semantic-task-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Use table-driven pure qualification tests and one fixture-backed command chain; keep all live provider calls in an explicit non-default lane, reuse existing scale and metrics coverage, and replace duplicate assertions instead of multiplying provider-model matrices." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-test-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-zero-paid-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Require independently current official provider terms, exact-model economics and exact-account-tier observations with bounded available quota, paid usage disabled, automatic overage disabled and a hard zero spend boundary; reject unknown, stale, paid, promotional and one-time-trial facts." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:provider-zero-paid-economics> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-profile-copy-on-write-work-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:selectionRule> "For one exact current provider profile basis, select exactly one matching admitted no-change receipt, Evidence and passing ProofResult; retain other profiles and bases as history." <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
<urn:usf:rule:provider-profile-copy-on-write-work-completion:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CompletionDerivationRule> <urn:usf:graph:provider-qualification> .
